course: dictionary
lesson: 427
title: One short word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are very short, and a short word can have many different meanings. «Ar» is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at where you read or heard it: a dialect, a science book, a computer game or a pirate story.
explain: In parts of northern England and the Midlands, «ar» means "yes", and it can also mean "our", as in «ar kid», which means my brother or sister. If someone says «Ar, let's go!» in a friendly local way, they mean yes.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. A chemistry text with the periodic table tells you Ar is a chemical symbol. A game with computer pictures over the real world tells you AR is augmented reality. Then check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: «Ar» on its own is not a standard English word, so context matters most.
fact: Ar is the chemical symbol for argon, a gas in the air that is used in light bulbs.
fact: AR is short for augmented reality, where a screen shows computer pictures over the real world. AR is also short for Arkansas, a US state.
fact: «Arr!» is how pirates talk in films and cartoons, and children shout it on Talk Like a Pirate Day.
fact: Ar is also the name of the letter R when you say it aloud.
exercise: A Yorkshire child says «Ar, I'll come with you.» What does ar mean here? | No | Arkansas | Argon | *Yes
exercise: In a science lesson, Ar is on the periodic table. What gas does Ar stand for? | Neon | Oxygen | Hydrogen | *Argon
exercise: «Grammar» ends in -ar, not -er. Which word also ends in -ar? | *grammar | teacher | water | paper
test: On Talk Like a Pirate Day, children shout «Arr!». What kind of sound is this? | A number | A question about the weather | *A pirate's shout | A sneeze
test: In an «AR game», what do you see on the screen? | A pirate ship with no sails | Only a blank screen | *Computer pictures shown over the real world | A list of spelling words
exam: A Lancashire friend says «Ar, let's go!» What does ar mean? | Argon | *Yes | Arkansas | No
